WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Good morning, Maureen and John and Nerdfighters.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.800
Today, we’re gonna talk about something 
that pisses me off.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.000
At the end of last year, there was a battle in the UK.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.900
The kid who won the X Factor, Joe McElderry,
who I know nothing about,

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.200
was apparently a shoo-in for the highest-selling artist in the UK Christmas charts.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:25.200
That is, until Rage Against the Machine decided to… rage against the machine…

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.200
and get a profanity-laden song from 1992 to the top of the UK charts.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.100
And they did it! Using an online anti-establishment social media thing,

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.400
Rage Against the Machine beat Joe McElderry by, like, 50,000 units,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.000
proving to the world that we’re not just sheep in a capitalist monarchy!

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.500
Except it turns out that we were raging against the wrong machine,

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:53.900
because Joe McElderry’s music is owned by the same people as Rage Against the Machine’s music.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.200
Sony Music owns both Sony BMG, which is Joe’s label,

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.800
and Epic Records, which is Rage Against the Machine’s label.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.400
So, while the anti-establishment folk were fighting their battles,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.100
Sony was laughing all the way to the bank,

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.900
and that is what I wanna talk about today – brands and their hypocrisy.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.900
Big corporations create these things called "brands"

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.800
so that they can sell more stuff to more people.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.000
They can use these brands to create specific marketing campaigns

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.800
to hit specific demographics of people who believe specific things.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:30.600
All the while, those big companies don’t give a crap about those “brand values”,

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.800
as long as the brands continue to make money.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:34.700
Don’t believe me?

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:38.000
So Dove, soap and skincare, those people, you know those people?

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.800
They have this great marketing campaign about how real women are beautiful.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.000
And that’s so great, and then you have a company like Axe Bodyspray.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.300
And Axe Bodyspray is like, “Shhhh! I’ll spray myself, and then I can use women for sex.”

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:55.700
And – I’m sure you know where I’m going with this – 
Axe and Dove are both owned by Unilever.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:00.100
Things get even crazier with media companies, because they own, like, 10,000 different properties.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:04.100
For example, the company that owns the UK softcore porn magazine Nuts

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:08.900
also owned the Hanna-Barbera cartoon franchise,
that company being Time Warner.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:13.900
MTV has a similar structure, owning both television channels for young children and horny men.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.900
I was personally extremely disappointed to find out

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:20.500
that the National Geographic channel is owned by the same people who run Fox freaking News!

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.800
Aaaagh!

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:27.600
Over here, you're talking about the beauty and wonder of natural and cultural diversity and the power of science,

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.100
and over here, you're Fox News!

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.400
*noises of confusion*

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.900
And food companies are no better.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:38.400
Kraft is busy boasting the importance of meatless meals with their Boca Burger franchise,

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:44.800
while simultaneously shilling both hot dogs and steak sauce to, quote, "SATISFY YOUR PRIMAL URGES!"

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.000
Kraft, until recently, was actually owned by Phillip Morris, the people who make Marlboro cigarettes,

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:53.300
which was possibly the most intense brand hypocrisy of all time,

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:58.000
with Kraft, focusing on family meals, and Philip Morris, focusing on... killing people.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.900
And Unilever, going back to the beginning, is doing it again with their food brands here,

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:05.100
offering up Slim-Fast with "keys to your weight loss success",

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.800
while pimping, like, twelve different ice cream companies,

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.800
including Breyers, Klondike Bar, Good Humor, and Ben and Jerry's,

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.400
and speaking of Ben and Jerry's,

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.500
aren't they supposed to be like the quirky, cute, independent ice cream company

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:19.600
for the independent-thinking, Cherry Garcia-loving, kinda-hippie person?

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.100
And now I found out that they're owned by, like, one of the biggest food companies in the world?

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.600
That's just depressing!

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.600
IT'S ALL LIES! LIIIIEEES!

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:29.300
*coughing*

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.500
It all comes down to this, folks -

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:36.200
there is only one corporate philosophy, only one set of brand values:

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.600
Make more money.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:43.600
If this means spending money to do good things so that more people will buy our stuff, then they will do that.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:47.600
But these big corporations do not have a conscience.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:53.200
They have one goal, one goal only, and sometimes it's easy to forget that.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.200
But it will always be true.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.200
Maureen, I will see you on Wednesday.

